A user wants this change: when #clear-filter is clicked: #seek is empty; every item in the list is visible again. Ensure typing in the filter still narrows the list.
Everything the page already does must keep working.

Explain how to do it, or give the updated page.

completion.text:
To achieve the desired functionality, we need to add a button with the ID `clear-filter` to the HTML and modify the JavaScript to handle the click event on this button. When the button is clicked, we will clear the value of the input field and set the `hidden` property of all list items to `false`, effectively showing all items again.

Here's the updated HTML:

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<head><title>s12</title></head>
<body>
<h2>s12</h2>
<input type="text" id="seek">
<button id="clear-filter">Clear Filter</button>
<ol id="results">
  <li class="item">tundra</li>
  <li class="item">tulip</li>
  <li class="item">meadow</li>
  <li class="item">canyon</li>
  <li class="item">delta</li>
</ol>
<script>
const model = { query: '' };
const field = document.getElementById('seek');
const rows = Array.from(document.querySelectorAll('#results .item'));
const clearFilterButton = document.getElementById('clear-filter');

function recompute() {
  model.query = field.value.toLowerCase();
  const q = model.query;
  rows.forEach(function (el) {
    const hit = el.textContent.toLowerCase().indexOf(q) !== -1;
    el.hidden = !hit;
  });
}

field.addEventListener('input', recompute);
clearFilterButton.addEventListener('click', function () {
  field.value = '';
  rows.forEach(function (el) {
    el.hidden = false;
  });
});
</script>
</body>
</html>
```

### Explanation:
1. **HTML Changes**:
   - Added a `<button>` element with the ID `clear-filter` next to the input field.
   - Added a `clearFilterButton` variable to reference the button element.

2. **JavaScript Changes**:
   - Added a `clearFilterButton` variable to reference the button element.
   - Added an event listener to the `clearFilterButton` that triggers the `recompute` function when clicked.
   - In the `recompute` function, we clear the value of the input field by setting `field.value = '';`.
   - We then set the `hidden` property of all list items to `false` using `rows.forEach(function (el) { el.hidden = false; })`.

This ensures that when the user clicks the "Clear Filter" button, the input field is cleared, and all items in the list are shown again. The typing in the filter still narrows the list as before.
